    "Psm"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Hear the right, O LORD, attend unto my cry, give ear unto my prayer, that goeth not out of feigned lips.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Let my sentence come forth from thy presence; let thine eyes behold the things that are equal.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "Thou hast proved mine heart; thou hast visited me in the night; thou hast tried me, and shalt find nothing; I am purposed that my mouth shall not transgress.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Concerning the works of men, by the word of thy lips I have kept me from the paths of the destroyer.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Hold up my goings in thy paths, that my footsteps slip not.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "I have called upon thee, for thou wilt hear me, O God: incline thine ear unto me, and hear my speech.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Shew thy marvellous lovingkindness, O thou that savest by thy right hand them which put their trust in thee from those that rise up against them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Keep me as the apple of the eye, hide me under the shadow of thy wings,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "From the wicked that oppress me, from my deadly enemies, who compass me about.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "They are inclosed in their own fat: with their mouth they speak proudly.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "They have now compassed us in our steps: they have set their eyes bowing down to the earth;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "Like as a lion that is greedy of his prey, and as it were a young lion lurking in secret places.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Arise, O LORD, disappoint him, cast him down: deliver my soul from the wicked, which is thy sword:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "From men which are thy hand, O LORD, from men of the world, which have their portion in this life, and whose belly thou fillest with thy hid treasure: they are full of children, and leave the rest of their substance to their babes.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:psalms:17:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "As for me, I will behold thy face in righteousness: I shall be satisfied, when I awake, with thy likeness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Psalms 17:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:psalms:17:15"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
